{"author":{"id":"85a3c31a64931f83958f26b24045fef8415ea6ff04d942d15661891c77fc0695"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794219367,"nonce":"f+lCB67cwXTlqZFqxfJOwSgejPE=","message":"Working tree (uncommitted):\n- MSL no longer uses naga's [[user(fake0)]] placeholders. It is written with wgpu-hal's Metal assignment (read from wgpu-hal 26.0.5's create_pipeline_layout): per stage, groups in order and bindings in order, buffers, textures and samplers each counting from 0, and the sizes buffer after the buffers when a storage buffer is bound or for a vertex stage; for a layout holding exactly the module's bindings, visible to every stage. So wgpu's passthrough MSL modules can take it unchanged.\n- Reflection::native reports each target's model: MSL slots per entry point with the sizes buffer, HLSL registers (naga's model: register = binding, space = group; samplers are indices into the group's sampler index buffer at t\u003cgroup\u003e, space255 over the heap at s0) and GLSL ES combined texture-samplers and uniform block names per entry point (from naga's GLSL ReflectionInfo). SPIR-V uses set = group, binding = binding.\n- tests/native.rs runs a corpus (tests/corpus: triangle, textures, compute with generics, f16, and Blinc's sdf_core as one module) through spirv-val (vulkan1.1), DXC (per entry point, 6.0 profiles, 6.2 with 16-bit types for f16), the Metal compiler (MSL 2.1) and glslangValidator. A missing compiler skips; RUSSL_REQUIRE_VALIDATORS makes it a failure. New CI job: Linux (apt spirv-tools and glslang-tools, DXC v1.9.2609 release) and macOS (the Metal toolchain via xcodebuild -downloadComponent when absent).\nLocally SPIR-V, DXC and glslang pass the whole corpus; the Metal toolchain is not downloaded on this machine, so Metal is checked in CI only.\n\nFound on the way: an array literal of unsuffixed elements was made concrete before its context was seen ([1, 2, 3] against [u32; 3] failed); it stays abstract now.","files":null}]}